    "suspected_causes": [
      "Sustained inbound probe filtering at international gateway level: all 4 ISP gateway TCP probes (TIC x2, Irancell, Asiatech) remain blocked — consistent across consecutive passes confirming intentional policy filtering not transient failure",
      "TIC gateway 1 (2.187.1.1) shifted from i/o timeout to 'connection refused' — active TCP RST indicates gateway is present and explicitly rejecting connections rather than silently dropping, same effective outcome but different mechanism",
      "IP range reachability stable at 3.2% (11/345 Iranian ranges responding from outside) — deliberate anti-monitoring posture persisting as established baseline",
      "Asiatech compound failure continues: gateway, web portal, and IP ranges all impaired — worst-affected ISP across all observed passes",
      "Electro DNS resolver unreachable again (persistent across passes) — possible targeted pressure on circumvention-adjacent DNS infrastructure",
      "Domestic payment layer showing improvement trend: Saman Bank latency dropped to 3188ms (from 3442ms last pass, 3962ms before that) suggesting load fluctuation not policy shift"
    ],
    "affected_services": [
      "All ISP management gateways (TIC x2, Irancell, Asiatech) — TCP probes uniformly blocked",
      "334 of 345 Iranian IP ranges unreachable from outside — MCI (AS197207), Irancell (AS44244), Shatel (AS31549) completely dark",
      "Asiatech — web portal, gateway, and IP ranges all impaired",
      "Electro DNS resolver — unreachable (persistent across passes)",
      "Snapp ride-hailing — redirect loop (persistent)",
      "Shaparak payment gateway — unreachable (persistent)",
      "Saman Bank — degraded response (3188ms, improved from 3442ms last pass)"
    ],
    "public_summary": "Iran's internet remains in partial outage with no material change since the last pass 10 minutes ago. All foreign platforms (Google, Telegram, YouTube, Instagram, WhatsApp, GitHub) and most domestic services (Digikala, Aparat, Tapsi, Filimo, CafeBazaar, Rubika, Eitaa) remain accessible. All ISP management gateways continue to block inbound probes, and Iranian IP range reachability from outside holds at approximately 3.2%. Circumvention tools (Tor, Snowflake, Psiphon) remain accessible. Saman Bank continues to improve in latency.",
    "insight": "The near-identical fingerprint across consecutive passes — zero ISP gateways reachable, 3.2% IP range reachability, all foreign platforms working, all circumvention tools accessible — confirms this is Iran's sustained anti-monitoring posture rather than any transient disruption; the network edge remains intentionally opaque to external probes while user-facing traffic flows normally, and the TIC gateway 1 shift from timeout to connection-refused is a minor behavioral variation within the same blocking regime.",
    "recommendation": "This stable pattern across multiple passes represents a confirmed operational baseline for Iran's anti-monitoring infrastructure. Shift monitoring focus to detection of deviation: a sudden improvement in IP range reachability or gateway responsiveness could signal a policy relaxation, while any foreign platform outage would indicate escalation into user-facing censorship. Consider adding traceroute probes to distinguish routing-level blocking from application-layer filtering at the gateways, and monitor IODA traffic volume for TIC (AS12880) to detect internal backbone changes invisible to external reachability probes."
  },
